error[RB0013]: `type` is a keyword and cannot be used as a field name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:1:12
  |
1 | type Evt { type: string }
  |            ^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are reserved; rename it, for example to `kind`

error[RB0013]: `fn` is a keyword and cannot be used as a field name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:3:3
  |
3 |   fn: int,
  |   ^^
  |
  = help: keywords are reserved; rename it, for example to `fnName`

error[RB0013]: `task` is a keyword and cannot be used as a field name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:4:3
  |
4 |   task: int
  |   ^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are reserved; rename it, for example to `taskName`

error[RB0013]: `error` is a keyword and cannot be used as a parameter name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:6:6
  |
6 | fn g(error: int) -> int
  |      ^^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are reserved; rename it, for example to `failure`

error[RB0013]: `event` is a keyword and cannot be used as a parameter name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:8:11
  |
8 | machine M(event: int) {
  |           ^^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are reserved; rename it, for example to `message`

error[RB0013]: `result` is reserved and cannot be used as a variable name
 --> RB0013-reserved-names.road:9:7
  |
9 |   var result: int = 0
  |       ^^^^^^
  |
  = help: `result` names an invoke's result inside `done`; choose another name

